EX 1(b): ARRAY + FOR LOOP + IF-ELSE + OPERATORS


AIM:

To write a Java program using an array, for loop, if-else statement, and operators to calculate the total and average of marks and determine whether each mark is Pass or Fail.


ALGORITHM:

1. Start the program.
2. Create an integer array containing the marks.
3. Initialize total to 0.
4. Use a for loop to traverse through each element of the array.
5. Add each mark to the total.
6. Check whether the mark is greater than or equal to 50.
7. If the mark is greater than or equal to 50, display "Pass".
8. Otherwise, display "Fail".
9. Calculate the average using total divided by the number of elements.
10. Display the total and average.
11. Stop the program.


SOURCE CODE:

public class MarksArray {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] m = {78, 91, 45, 66, 88};
        int total = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < m.length; i++) {

            total = total + m[i];

            if (m[i] >= 50)
                System.out.println(m[i] + " Pass");
            else
                System.out.println(m[i] + " Fail");
        }

        double avg = total / (double) m.length;

        System.out.println("Total = " + total);
        System.out.println("Average = " + avg);
    }
}


OUTPUT:

78 Pass
91 Pass
45 Fail
66 Pass
88 Pass
Total = 368
Average = 73.6
